  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\left(\\cot \\alpha_1\\right)\\left(\\cot \\alpha_2\\right) \\ldots \\ldots .\\left(\\cot \\alpha_n\\right)=1,0  < \\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\ldots . . \\alpha_n < \\pi / 2$, then the maximum value of $\\left(\\cos a_1\\right)\\left(\\cos \\alpha_2\\right) \\ldots \\ldots$ $\\left(\\cos \\alpha_n\\right)$ is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2^{n / 2}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2^n}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 n}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\left(\\cos \\alpha_1 \\cos \\alpha_2 \\ldots . \\cos \\alpha_n\\right)^2}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(1+\\tan ^2 \\alpha_1\\right)\\left(1+\\tan ^2 \\alpha_2\\right) \\ldots \\ldots\\left(1+\\tan ^2 \\alpha_n\\right) \\\\\n&\\geq\\left(2 \\tan \\alpha_1\\right)\\left(2 \\tan \\alpha_2\\right) \\ldots \\ldots .\\left(2 \\tan \\alpha_n\\right)[\\text { AM }-\\text { GM inequality } \\\\\n&=2^n \\times \\frac{1}{\\cot \\alpha_1 \\cot \\alpha_2 \\ldots . . \\cot \\alpha_n}=2^n \\\\\n&\\therefore \\cos \\alpha_1 \\cos \\alpha_2 \\ldots . . \\cos \\alpha_n \\leq \\frac{1}{2^{n / 2}}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}